cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyAgent in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PyAgent: Spec-Driven Architecture for Orchestrating Multi-Agent Systems"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PyAgent Team"
    email: team@pyagent.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/pyagent-core/pyagent"
url: "https://pyagent.org"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  PyAgent is a spec-driven architecture for orchestrating multi-agent LLM
  systems, organized around four independently adoptable pillars: Blueprint
  (declarative YAML specification, compiled onto any registered runtime
  adapter), Execution & Routing (18 named orchestration patterns with
  difficulty-aware model routing), Context & Memory (three-tier memory with
  a trust-aware context ledger), and Observability (pattern-aware
  OpenTelemetry tracing with a web dashboard).
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent orchestration
  - large language models
  - declarative architecture
  - spec-driven development
  - OpenTelemetry
